{"id":"moons","title":"Largest moons","prompt":"Name the 10 largest moons in the Solar System by radius","noun":"moons","category":"Science","metric":"Mean radius","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of natural satellites","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_natural_satellites","asOf":"2026-11-04"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Ganymede","aliases":["Jupiter III","Ganymede moon","Jovian Moon Ganymede","Satellite Ganymede","Jovian Satellite Ganymede","Ganymedean atmosphere","Jupiter III Ganymede","J III Ganymede","Jovian Satellite III Ganymede","Magnetic field of Ganymede"],"value":"2,634.1 km","n":2634.1,"article":"Ganymede (moon)","fact":{"text":"Jupiter's largest moon is the only one in the Solar System with its own internally generated magnetic field.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ganymede_(moon)"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Titan","aliases":["Saturni Luna","Saturn VI","Titan moon","Moon titan","Saturnian Moon Titan","Satellite Titan","Saturnian Satellite Titan","S VI Titan","Saturn VI Titan","Saturnian Satellite VI Titan"],"value":"2,574.73 km","n":2574.73,"article":"Titan (moon)","fact":{"text":"From its surface, Saturn looks more than ten times as large as the Moon does from Earth.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titan_(moon)"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Callisto","aliases":["Jupiter IV","Callisto moon","Callisto the moon","Jovian Moon Callisto","Satellite Callisto","Callistoan atmosphere","J IV Callisto","Jupiter IV Callisto","Jovian Satellite Callisto","Jovian Satellite IV Callisto"],"value":"2,410.3 km","n":2410.3,"article":"Callisto (moon)","fact":{"text":"A moon of Jupiter, its surface is the oldest and most heavily cratered in the Solar System.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Callisto_(moon)"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Io","aliases":["Jupiter I","Io moon","Volcano moon","Jovian Moon Io","Satellite Io","Lo","Ionian atmosphere","J I Io","Jupiter I Io","Jovian Satellite Io","Jovian Satellite I Io"],"value":"1,821.6 km","n":1821.6,"ar